<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qutlugh Terken Khatun</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1282</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qutlugh Terken Khatun was ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerman">Kerman</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> from 1257 to 1282, the widow of the Qutlugh-Khanid ruler Qutb al-Din Muhammad. Governing as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a>, she was remembered for justice, irrigation works and building. Her daughter <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/padishah-khatun">Padishah Khatun</a> married the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhan">Ilkhan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abaqa-khan">Abaqa</a> and later ruled Kerman herself.</p></div>
